# CloudAccounts — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; never commit
# real keys. Only variables prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ reach the browser.
#
# These three are the whole required set. The site runs with none of them —
# content comes from the typed modules in src/content and submissions are held
# in memory — but a PRODUCTION server refuses to start in that state rather
# than silently dropping enquiries.
#
# Optional integrations (transactional email, automation webhooks, analytics)
# are listed in the README under "Optional integrations". None is required,
# and each degrades cleanly when absent: email is logged to the server console
# instead of sent, webhooks are skipped, analytics stays dormant.
#
# See docs/SUPABASE-SETUP.md for migrations, seeding and the security tests.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (Supabase)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project Settings → API. Either key format works: the newer
# sb_publishable_… / sb_secret_… pair, or the legacy anon / service_role JWTs.
#
# The anon key is safe to expose ONLY because Row Level Security is enforced
# on every table — that is what 0002_rls.sql establishes.
#
# The service role key BYPASSES RLS entirely. It must never be prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never be imported into a client component, and never be
# committed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
